  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia: Alternative Dispute Resolution Somalia  Programme - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To improve processes for alternative dispute resolution (ADR) mechanisms in the targeted areas by improving capacity of the ADR units and Centres to provide efficient and human rights compliant services to the Somali population and improving awareness of justice seekers, especially vulnerable groups, of how to claim their rights through the ADR Centres. 2) To improve processes for the referral of GBV survivors and affected communities by improving the capacity of local justice actors and networks to support this referral.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Federal Ministry of Justice, State Ministry of Justice, Judiciary, Police, Attorney General&#x2019;s Offices, civil society and legal aid organizations.
Indirect beneficiaries: Somali population, specifically women, girls, survivors of gender-based violence (GBV) and those at risk of GBV, internally displaced persons, youth, religious leaders, community elders, rural communities and minority social groups.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aimed to improve access to formal as well as customary and informal justice for all Somalis, especially women and vulnerable groups.</narrative>
  </description>
